<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Sacred War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">24–26 June <a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Священная война, Svyashchennaya voyna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;The Sacred War&quot; is one of the best-known Soviet songs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> as the Great Patriotic War. Two days after the German invasion, on 24 June 1941, its words appeared at the same time in the newspapers Izvestia and Krasnaya Zvezda, signed by the poet Vasily Lebedev-Kumach.</p></div>
